  "description": "Google reCAPTCHA token verification for .NET APIs: the IRecaptchaService contract, the Google siteverify implementation, a switched-off implementation, options with startup validation, and BusinessException errors (400 RECAPTCHA__INVALID_TOKEN, 503 RECAPTCHA__VERIFICATION_UNAVAILABLE).",
  "id": "BusinessFeatures.Recaptchas",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-16T03:42:42.46Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "vY3Po8+ZXwiSOtO+TH3P2tBzhMWeBJucg+4FuyPArntUTizWN/ZIPXpNtZZQn9pqE1BkfMFrGPwspiFp0HUGIA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 36739,
  "published": "2026-11-16T03:39:11.93Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BusinessFeatures.Recaptchas 9.0.0 is the first release. It is extracted from the iot-vn authentication service, where it was the reCAPTCHA check of the Users module, and copied with the same behaviour: IRecaptchaService, GoogleRecaptchaService (one call to Google siteverify, 10 s timeout, no retry, overridable IsAccepted), DisabledRecaptchaService, RecaptchaOptions (SiteKey, SecretKey, Enabled = true, MinimumScore = 0.5) with startup validation, AddApplicationRecaptcha, and the BusinessExceptions InvalidRecaptchaTokenException (400 RECAPTCHA__INVALID_TOKEN) and RecaptchaVerificationUnavailableException (503 RECAPTCHA__VERIFICATION_UNAVAILABLE). Only the namespaces changed, and Google's answer is now read with System.Text.Json, so no host JSON serializer is needed. Builds for net9.0 and net10.0. Enabled = false accepts every request without any check.",
